{
  "description": "Errors shared by the containers operations, observed on the live API while the SDK used a hand-written containers model (2026-09-30 to 2026-11-02). Codes: 7003 Could not route; 1609 APPLICATION_NOT_FOUND; 1607 DURABLE_OBJECT_NOT_CONTAINER_ENABLED; 1608 DURABLE_OBJECT_ALREADY_HAS_APPLICATION; 1000 while checking the application Durable Object; HTTP 400 when a just-created Durable Object namespace is not yet visible; `can't create application at this time` on create, which succeeds when retried. Image preparation: POST /accounts/{account_id}/containers/image-preparations rejects an unpinned image with HTTP 400, code 1000, message {\"error\":\"image must be digest-pinned and hosted in a supported managed registry\"}; a nonexistent managed digest returns HTTP 400, code 1000, message {\"error\":\"image does not exist in this account\"}; a missing image field returns HTTP 400, code 1602, VALIDATE_INPUT, which stays BadRequest. ContainerImagePreparationsService documents HTTP 403 with no code, so it stays Forbidden (https://github.com/cloudflare/workers-sdk/blob/main/packages/containers-shared/src/client/services/ContainerImagePreparationsService.ts).",
  "patches": [
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/shapes/com.cloudflare.containers#InvalidRoute",
      "value": {
        "type": "structure",
        "members": {
